{"tool_name":"hasappy","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"hasappy","home":"https://github.com/gdiminin/HaSAPPy","license":"MIT","summary":"A tool for analyzing NGS datasets form pooled haploid mammalian cell screens. It is used to identify insertion locations in the whole genome, map them at the level of genes, and classify insertions according to their effects on gene function.","addition_date":"2018-06-25T11:15:57Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T13:46:17.306048Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:hasappy","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"giulio.diminin@biol.ethz.ch","name":"Giulio Di Minin","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"note":"Tutorial material","type":["Training material"],"url":"https://github.com/gdiminin/HaSAPPy/blob/master/docs/Tutorials/RunningHaSAPPyWorkflowsScript.md"},{"note":"Tutorial material","type":["Training material"],"url":"https://github.com/gdiminin/HaSAPPy/blob/master/docs/Tutorials/TestRunHaSAPPY.md"},{"type":["General"],"url":"https://github.com/gdiminin/HaSAPPy/blob/master/README.md"},{"type":["General"],"url":"https://github.com/gdiminin/HaSAPPy/tree/master/docs"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Data reference","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2093"},"format":[{"term":"Raw sequence format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2571"}]},{"data":{"term":"Nucleic acid sequence (raw)","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2975"},"format":[{"term":"Raw sequence format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2571"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Gene functional annotation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3672"},{"term":"Sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2403"},{"term":"Variant classification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3225"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Genotype/phenotype report","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0920"},"format":[{"term":"Textual format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2330"}]}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"HaSAPPy","operating_system":["Linux"],"owner":"ELIXIR-EE","publication":[{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pcbi.1005950","metadata":{"abstract":"Haploid cells are increasingly used for screening of complex pathways in animal genomes. Hemizygous mutations introduced through viral insertional mutagenesis can be directly selected for phenotypic changes. Here we present HaSAPPy a tool for analysing sequencing datasets of screens using insertional mutations in large pools of haploid cells. Candidate gene prediction is implemented through identification of enrichment of insertional mutations after selection by simultaneously evaluating several parameters. We have developed HaSAPPy for analysis of genetic screens for silencing factors of X chromosome inactivation in haploid mouse embryonic stem cells. To benchmark the performance, we further analyse several datasets of genetic screens in human haploid cells for which candidates have been validated. Our results support the effective candidate prediction strategy of HaSAPPy. HaSAPPy is implemented in Python, licensed under the MIT license, and is available from https://github.com/gdiminin/HaSAPPy.","authors":[{"name":"Di Minin G."},{"name":"Postlmayr A."},{"name":"Wutz A."}],"citationCount":9,"date":"2018-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"PLoS Computational Biology","title":"HaSAPPy: A tool for candidate identification in pooled forward genetic screens of haploid mammalian cells"},"pmcid":"PMC5798846","pmid":"29337991"}],"topic":[{"term":"Function analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_1775"},{"term":"Genotype and phenotype","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0625"},{"term":"Sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0080"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"HaSAPPy","home":"https://bio.tools/hasappy","license":"MIT","summary":"A tool for analyzing NGS datasets form pooled haploid mamma